N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): the clip's sustained part (harmonic/percussive separation) was pitch-tracked for the call (0.3-5.0 s: A4, then D5 D5 B4 B4 C sharp 5 C sharp 5 A4 A4, twice, each note struck twice at 0.31 s); from 5.05 s every beat (0.975 s) was reduced to its strongest pitches and matched to major and minor triads, giving the sequence D D D | G Bm A D | G Bm A D | D D | G Bm A D | G Bm A D | D D, with the low pipes on G3, B2, A2 and D3. In each beat the band strikes twice, on the beat and 0.26-0.33 s later.
N:INTONATION: the pipes sit about 20 cents sharp of A=440 overall, and the chords drift a little through the clip.
N:UNCERTAIN: the first chord of each phrase (G and B sound with E: G with an added sixth, or E minor; a pipe between G and G sharp is heard at 21.6 s); whether the chord on B is B minor or a D chord over B; the B flat that sounds against the D chords; the inner voicing (written plainly); whether the call is the start of the piece.
